## Assumptions &amp; Methodology

<div class="cf-assumptions reveal">
  <h3>How this forecast was built</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Revenue baseline:</strong> 5-month average January–May 2026 ($573,394 ÷ 5 = $114,679/month). This period is used in preference to the full FY average as it reflects the current, higher revenue run rate (income up 33.5% vs prior half-year).</li>
    <li><strong>NET30 payment terms:</strong> Confirmed by invoice register — INV-2026-051, -058 and -060 all carry exactly 30 days from issue to due date. Cash inflows in month N = billings from month N−1. All income streams (Consulting, Datasights On Charge, Admin Fee) are modelled on this timing.</li>
    <li><strong>Outstanding receivables ($186,285):</strong> Modelled as collected over three months: $100,000 in June (known large invoices), $60,000 in July (remaining overdue), $26,285 in August (balance). Collection front-loaded based on recency — most invoices are only 9 days overdue.</li>
    <li><strong>Payables:</strong> Effectively nil ($0.00 outstanding). No payables clearance required.</li>
    <li><strong>3-pay month — July 2026:</strong> Fortnightly Friday payroll falls on 3 Jul, 17 Jul, and 31 Jul — three pay runs. Extra wages = one additional fortnight = $18,401. Q4 FY26 super (due 28 July) accrued in monthly figures; cash timing to be confirmed against payroll records.</li>
    <li><strong>Expenses:</strong> Monthly averages from Jan–May 2026 Xero P&L. Fixed costs (rent, super, contractors) treated as stable. No capital expenditure or known one-off costs included beyond what appears in the operating expense lines.</li>
    <li><strong>Financial year:</strong> GemCutter FY runs 1 July – 30 June. This forecast covers the first five months of FY2027 (July–November 2026) plus the final month of FY2026 (June 2026). Tax timing for end-of-FY items should be confirmed separately.</li>
    <li><strong>Data current to:</strong> 26 May 2026. Xero last refreshed 26 May 2026 10:19 AEST.</li>
  </ul>
</div>

